    subtitle: 'The Engineering Calculator Center: how to find a calculator, how every calculator reads your numbers, validates them, rounds and explains its result, how to remember, copy and save results, a tour of the nine disciplines with hand-checked examples, and the limits you should know about.',
    appTitle: '',
    preface: [
      'The Calculator Center gathers every calculator in the Pocket Technical Reference in one searchable place. Dozens of calculators sit in the chapters where their subject is explained; the Center lists them together, sorted by name, filtered by discipline and found by a search box that looks at the title, the description, keywords and the labels of the inputs. Because every calculator shares one framework, learning the framework once teaches you all of them.',
      'The calculators are ordinary program logic, so this book does not ask you to take anything on trust. The examples run the app’s own calculators on stated inputs, work the same answer out independently in the book’s own code (a formula, a hand calculation or a counting rule) and show the two side by side with a tick or a cross. If they ever disagreed, the example would print MISMATCH. Where a constant had to be assumed, such as the atmospheric pressure used to turn gauge pressure into absolute, the example says so.',
      'The calculators are educational estimates. They are not a substitute for the governing code, standard, product data sheet or a qualified professional, and the financial calculators are teaching tools, not advice. Each lesson has objectives, an explanation, key points, worked examples and review questions; the book ends with problems, a 20-question exam and a glossary. A late lesson reports an honest audit of what the calculators do when a field is set to zero or to a negative number.'
    ],
    audience: 'Anyone who uses the calculators and wants to know exactly how they read inputs, check them and present results, and anyone learning how a field of small engineering calculators can be built to be consistent.',
