          'When you type a search, results are ordered by how well the term matches. The best tier is an exact match of the term or of one of its abbreviations. Next comes a term that starts with your words, then a term with a word that starts with them, then a term or abbreviation that contains them, then a term that contains every word separately, and last an entry that matched only through its definitions or aliases. Within a tier, terms are in alphabetical order.',
          'This is why typing a term name puts that term first and entries that merely mention it later. A short abbreviation such as “psi” or “NPSH” goes to the top when it is exactly an abbreviation of a term.'
