          'Because entries are harvested from many chapters, wording and depth vary: some definitions are one line, some are several sentences with units and examples. A definition is not a specification; limits, tolerances and requirements belong to the governing standard or data sheet. When two definitions seem to disagree, they are probably for different subjects or conditions; the source section will usually show which.'
